<title>SINGAPORE: Hong Kong's Yue Hwa opens S$49 mln Singapore store.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong's Yue Hwa opens S$49 mln Singapore store.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong-based Chinese products retailer Yue Hwa Group said on Wednesday it has invested Singapore $49.35 million in a Singapore department store.</p>
<p>The new store has 50,000 sq feet of retail space over six floors and is located in the heart of Singapore's Chinatown in Eu Tong Sen Street, Yue Hwa said in a statement. Including Singapore, Yue Hwa has a total of seven stores.</p>
<p>The Singapore store, which had a soft opening on Wednesday, is Yue Hwa's second outside Hong Kong, after Beijing in China.</p>
<p>Yue Hwa recorded a turnover of S$151 million in 1994/1995.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
